## Tutorials

Information can be passed to methods as a parameter. Parameters act as variables inside the method.

Parameters are specified after the method name, inside the parentheses.
You can add as many parameters as you want, just separate them with a comma.

The following example has a 
method that takes aStringcalledfnameas parameter.
When the method is called, we pass along a first name,
which is used inside the method to print the full name:

You can have as many parameters as you like:

It is common to useif...elsestatements inside methods:

### Code Examples

```
Example
public class Main {
  static void myMethod(String fname) {
    System.out.println(fname + " Refsnes");
  }

  public static void main(String[] args) {
    myMethod("Liam");
    myMethod("Jenny");
    myMethod("Anja");
  }
}
// Liam Refsnes
// Jenny Refsnes
// Anja Refsnes
Try it Yourself »

